                            <comment id="503243" author="JIRAUSER19208" created="Mon, 12 Oct 2026 18:08:52 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I reproduced this on 2.17.59. --dirty --archive-id 1 returns 0 on a file with no HSM flags, but the flags stay unchanged. --dirty alone returns EINVAL.&lt;br/&gt;
The missing-HS_EXISTS check in mdt_hsm_state_set() exits with rc still at 0. Changed that line to return -EINVAL.&lt;br/&gt;
Rebuilt and loaded the patched MDT module. The same request now returns 22 and leaves the flags unchanged. Setting --exists --archive-id 32 still works.&lt;br/&gt;
Also added a check to sanity-hsm test 1c and ran it:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;code panel&quot; style=&quot;border-width: 1px;&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;codeContent panelContent&quot;&gt;
&lt;pre class=&quot;code-java&quot;&gt;
PASS 1c (2s)
&lt;/pre&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There were some SSH and copytool cleanup warnings during setup that I still need to sort out in my lab, but test 1c passed, including the existing archive-ID checks.&lt;br/&gt;
Patch attached.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
